<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>North American Migration Patterns (3000 BC - 1492 AD)</name><description>A visualization of major historical migration and expansion patterns in North America prior to European contact.</description><Style id="style_ancestral_puebloans"><LineStyle><color>ff0000ff</color><width>3</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>400000ff</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="style_mississippians"><LineStyle><color>ff00ff00</color><width>3</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>4000ff00</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="style_athabaskan"><LineStyle><color>ffff0000</color><width>3</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>40ff0000</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="style_algonquian"><LineStyle><color>ff00ffff</color><width>3</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>4000ffff</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="style_inuit"><LineStyle><color>ffffffff</color><width>3</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>40ffffff</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="style_uto_aztecan"><LineStyle><color>ff800080</color><width>3</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>40800080</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="style_haudenosaunee"><LineStyle><color>ff00a5ff</color><width>3</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>4000a5ff</color></PolyStyle></Style><Placemark><name>Athabaskan Migration (Dene/Apache/Navajo)</name><description>The southward migration of Athabaskan speakers from Northwest Canada/Alaska into the Southwest (approx. 1000-1400 AD).</description><styleUrl>#style_athabaskan</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-125,60 -115,50 -110,40 -106,35</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ancestral Puebloan Expansion</name><description>Expansion and consolidation of farming communities in the Four Corners region (approx. 900-1300 AD).</description><styleUrl>#style_ancestral_puebloans</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-110,38 -108,37 -107,35 -109,34</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mississippian Culture Expansion</name><description>Spread of mound-building cultures and maize agriculture from the Mississippi River Valley (approx. 800-1400 AD).</description><styleUrl>#style_mississippians</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-90,35 -85,34 -82,32 -80,33</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Thule (Inuit) Migration</name><description>The rapid eastward migration of Thule people from Alaska across the Arctic to Greenland (approx. 1000-1300 AD).</description><styleUrl>#style_inuit</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-160,70 -120,70 -80,70 -50,70</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Uto-Aztecan Movement</name><description>Migration of Uto-Aztecan speakers from the Great Basin southward into Central Mexico (Nahua/Aztec ancestors).</description><styleUrl>#style_uto_aztecan</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-115,40 -110,30 -105,25 -99,19</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Algonquian Expansion</name><description>The movement of Algonquian speakers from the Great Lakes region towards the Atlantic Coast.</description><styleUrl>#style_algonquian</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-85,45 -80,43 -75,40 -72,41</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Iroquoian (Haudenosaunee) Consolidation</name><description>The formation of the Iroquois Confederacy in the Northeast (approx. 1100-1450 AD).</description><styleUrl>#style_haudenosaunee</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-79,43 -77,43 -75,43 -74,43</coordinates></LineString></Placemark></Document></kml>